## Acceptance tests

- [ ] Offline: compose and queue both email and Sidequest messages. No network required.
- [ ] Online: email outbox flushes via SMTP. Message appears in provider's Sent.
- [ ] Two devices: Sidequest message A→B with only tailcat-rs (no SMTP involved).
- [ ] App restart: outbox, identities, and local store survive.
- [ ] Eject account: all local data for that account is gone from disk.
- [ ] No network calls to any Sidequest-owned host. Only user's mail hosts + DERP (if sidequest path active).
- [ ] Kill tailcat-rs (simulate panic): email path continues to function.
- [ ] `grep -r "telemetry\|analytics\|phone.home\|update.check" src/` returns nothing.
- [ ] `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` at crate root.   
